ve_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\nv4.5.dev2.official [af2c713]\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.5.dev2\n\n### Issue description\n\nI’ve noticed this since older versions, but now I’d like to point it out clearly. I’m not sure what the intended behavior is, but my assumption is that when you're renaming, the input field is designed to follow you - so you can scroll further down the list and still continue renaming. I also believe this approach is easier than placing an input field on every line in the tree.\n\nHowever, there are position-related issues. For example, the input field can move outside the line being renamed and appear in the wrong position, which confuses the user. Also, if you select an item and move the cursor using the arrow keys, then scroll the list, the input field shifts to an incorrect location as well.\n\nOverall, I think the correct behavior for this element should be to stay within the bounds of the line being renamed, or stick to the bottom of the list if it has been scrolled far down.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nhttps://youtu.be/d45idu_Xjmg\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n--","closed_by":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"